{"record":"parent_entry","position":{"parent_record":"request:00000000000000000035:0000","subposition":null},"original_role":"tool","source":"tool_result","trust":"untrusted","provenance":null,"content":"{\"kind\":\"tool_result\",\"call_id\":\"call_01a16a17a575744388e5afdb3810cf0d\",\"output\":\"{\\n  \\\"chunk_id\\\": \\\"exec-11-1\\\",\\n  \\\"exit_code\\\": 0,\\n  \\\"terminal_status\\\": \\\"completed\\\",\\n  \\\"output\\\": \\\"infra-pilot : 2 commits touching\\\\r\\\\nstreuland : 2 commits touching\\\\r\\\\nforgecms : 2 commits touching\\\\r\\\\nForgeCMS : 1 commits touching\\\\r\\\\nai-chat-webui : 2 commits touching\\\\r\\\\nstranded-horizons : 2 commits touching\\\\r\\\\ncooperating-screen : 2 commits touching\\\\r\\\\ned-docs : 2 commits touching\\\\r\\\\naktienwerk : 0 commits touching\\\\r\\\\nforum-for-nerds : 1 commits touching\\\\r\\\\n===5854be7 latest===\\\\r\\\\ncommit 5854be735317856d537899340de47f376aa3ac4e\\\\r\\\\nAuthor: Daniel Rosemann <daniel.rosemann10@gmail.com>\\\\r\\\\nDate:   Fri Oct 23 20:44:02 2026 +0200\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n    Add forum-for-nerds merge\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\ndiff --git a/README.md b/README.md\\\\r\\\\nindex 137d7cd..ee04dfb 100644\\\\r\\\\n--- a/README.md\\\\r\\\\n+++ b/README.md\\\\r\\\\n@@ -25,6 +25,7 @@ Since 10 September 2023 I've been part of Emergency Response: Crestwood County,\\\\r\\\\n I also built a Raspberry Pi AI plant monitoring project with sensors and AI, and I spend time on hardware hacking and AI security.\\\\r\\\\n After over 2,000 gaming videos I made 15 videos in the Theo Browne style, archived at https://github.com/drosemann/drosemann/tree/main/theo-browne-era-video-style\\\\r\\\\n All of my domains are with netcup: d5niel.de for my portfolio, which will run on ForgeCMS in the future, shadowunity.de for my Minecraft server, and hosting-club.de, a former hosting forum.\\\\r\\\\n+Over the years every hosting era also produced a forum or blog attempt, ten in total, and I finally merged all of them into one codebase: forum-for-nerds, a self-hosted Next.js forum plus blog running on pure Docker with SQLite for dev and MariaDB in prod. Ten dead forums walked in, one nerd forum walked out.\\\\r\\\\n For storage I ended up with OneDrive 365 Basic with 100 GB for 2 euros a month, after years of being convinced I'd never give Microsoft a cent, until the Windows and Samsung integration won me over.\\\\r\\\\n Speed doesn't matter much to me, and if OneDrive ever offers a 500 GB cold archive tier on very slow old hard drives for one or two euros a month, I'd be the first customer, and I'd probably store all my photos there too since 100 GB is easily enough for me.\\\\r\\\\n I never actually needed it, since I never used more than two or three GB, but now I just upload 30 GB so I can say I use it.\\\\r\\\\n===CURRENT mentions check===\\\\r\\\\ninfra-pilot in current: True\\\\r\\\\nstreuland in current: False\\\\r\\\\nforgecms in current: True\\\\r\\\\nForgeCMS in current: True\\\\r\\\\nai-chat-webui in current: False\\\\r\\\\nstranded-horizons in current: False\\\\r\\\\ncooperating-screen in current: False\\\\r\\\\ned-docs in current: False\\\\r\\\\naktienwerk in current: False\\\\r\\\\nforum-for-nerds in current: True\\\\r\\\\n===OLDEST README===\\\\r\\\\n- 👋 Hi, I’m @DaaanielTV\\\\r\\\\n- 👀 I’m interested in tech and ai\\\\r\\\\n- 🌱 I’m currently learning python and java\\\\r\\\\n- 💞️ I’m looking to collaborate on my minecraft server\\\\r\\\\n- 📫 How to reach me discord: daaanieltv\\\\r\\\\n- 😄 Pronouns: he/his\\\\r\\\\n- ⚡ Fun fact: doing stuff with debian since 2018\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n<!---\\\\r\\\\nDaaanielTV/DaaanielTV is a ✨ special ✨ repository because its `README.md` (this file) appears on your GitHub profile.\\\\r\\\\nYou can click the Preview link to take a look at your changes.\\\\r\\\\n--->\\\\r\\\\n\\\",\\n  \\\"original_output_bytes\\\": 3007,\\n  \\\"original_output_tokens\\\": 752,\\n  \\\"truncated\\\": false\\n}\"}","truncated":false}
{"record":"parent_entry","position":{"parent_record":"6c0a5461-375c-5093-988b-fd1da6052eab:0000","subposition":null},"original_role":"tool","source":"tool_result","trust":"untrusted","provenance":null,"content":"{\"kind\":\"tool_result\",\"call_id\":\"call_01a16a1700ba76b0b5ca0bcb26e5b3e2\",\"output\":\"{\\n  \\\"chunk_id\\\": \\\"exec-6-1\\\",\\n  \\\"exit_code\\\": 0,\\n  \\\"terminal_status\\\": \\\"completed\\\",\\n  \\\"output\\\": \\\"[unified exec output: 1 invalid UTF-8 byte replaced with U+FFFD]\\\\nCOUNT: 10\\\\r\\\\nai-chat-webui | JavaScript | ?0 | A privacy-focused AI chat web interface powered by Ollama local models, with fast streaming responses and a responsive UI.\\\\r\\\\naktienwerk | Python | ?0 | Automated SEC filings, stock prices, and easy-to-understand explanations for 100 U.S. companies�?\\\\\\\"using only Python's standard library and SQLite, no Bloomberg.\\\\r\\\\ncooperating-screen | Dart | ?0 | A cross-device screen sharing project built with Flutter, WebRTC, and a Node.js signaling service, including pairing and session management.\\\\r\\\\ndrosemann |  | ?0 | Your GitHub profile/config repository, used for profile setup and metadata\\\\r\\\\ned-docs | TypeScript | ?0 | Offline-first Markdown writing with the precision of ed and the comfort of modern docs.\\\\r\\\\nforgecms | HTML | ?0 | A modern blog/CMS system built with Flask and MariaDB, featuring auth, admin content management, Markdown posts, image uploads, and SEO-friendly URLs.\\\\r\\\\nforum-for-nerds | TypeScript | ?0 | Ten dead forums walked in. One nerd forum walked out.\\\\r\\\\ninfra-pilot | TypeScript | ?2 | Infra Pilot manages your own VPS and container fleet\\\\r\\\\nstranded-horizons | JavaScript | ?0 | A lightweight browser survival game built with vanilla HTML, CSS, and JavaScript where you survive enemy waves, earn coins, and buy upgrades.\\\\r\\\\nstreuland | Java | ?1 | An open-source Paper plugin for managing player plots in a vanilla-style Minecraft world, with protected plots, district progression, and a marketplace.\\\\r\\\\n===LOCAL PARENT===\\\\r\\\\nai-chat-webui | readme=True\\\\r\\\\naktienwerk | readme=True\\\\r\\\\ncooperating-screen | readme=True\\\\r\\\\ndrosemann | readme=True\\\\r\\\\ned-docs | readme=True\\\\r\\\\nforgecms | readme=True\\\\r\\\\nforum-for-nerds | readme=True\\\\r\\\\ninfra-pilot | readme=True\\\\r\\\\nstranded-horizons | readme=True\\\\r\\\\nstreuland | readme=True\\\\r\\\\n===CURRENT README===\\\\r\\\\nHey, I'm Daniel, a dev by passion from near Frankfurt am Main, a hosting nerd and AI tinkerer, and currently in my second year of training as an IT specialist for system integration.\\\\nI live for technology, IT infrastructure and artificial intelligence, and learning by doing is my thing because I'd rather build servers than slide decks.\\\\nI've been active in the Minecraft and hosting community for years, and since 22 April 2018 I've been running my Minecraft server ShadowUnity.\\\\nFor my own projects I use my private stack, while at work I use the stack required there.\\\\nMy full stack work covers HTML, CSS, JavaScript, Java, PHP, Python and React and TUI development.\\\\nMy infrastructure work covers Docker, Linux, NGINX, Apache, Proxmox, Velocity and KVM with libvirt.\\\\nI have a lot of experience with the Pterodactyl and Coolify panels, but for my own services I now prefer pure Docker because it means less overhead and more control.\\\\nI have a lot of productive experience with MariaDB and I've tested Supabase extensively, both in the cloud and self hosted.\\\\nI use Cloudflare for DNS, HetrixTools for monitoring, Trello and Notion for project management for ShadowUnity, and Vercel for automatic deployments.\\\\nOn the client side I use Windows, with a nod to the games industry, and I plan to switch to Linux as soon as anticheat support gets better.\\\\nMy focus is on cybersecurity, AI, cloud and virtualization, and automation with Python.\\\\nMy hosting path went from Aternos to Ploudos to Minehub, which later closed.\\\\nAfter that it went through DeinServerHost, Strato, Host-Unlimited, LuxVPS and Mine-Hoster.\\\\nI cancelled ST-Hosting after one month because their LXC setup didn't meet my expectations, and HT-Hosting went insolvent, which taught me to migrate under time pressure.\\\\nI used Index Hosting until mid March and cancelled it because thei…","truncated":true}
